      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-persuasion-concession-01",
        "title": "Persuasion & Concession: part 1",
        "setting": "quiet cafe",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "requests",
        "characters": [
          "Nora",
          "Samir"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Nora",
            "text": "What is the practical implication of that point?",
            "translation_fa": "پیامد عملی اون نکته چیه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Samir",
            "text": "A persuasive case becomes stronger when it acknowledges the most reasonable objection rather than pretending none exists.",
            "translation_fa": "یک استدلال قانع‌کننده وقتی قوی‌تر می‌شه که منطقی‌ترین ایراد رو بپذیره، نه اینکه وانمود کنه ایرادی وجود نداره."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Nora",
            "text": "Does the evidence justify going that far?",
            "translation_fa": "آیا شواهد واقعاً چنین نتیجه‌ای رو توجیه می‌کنه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 4,
            "speaker": "Samir",
            "text": "I would make one concession here: the proposal is costly in the short term, even if the longer-term case remains compelling.",
            "translation_fa": "اینجا یک نکته رو می‌پذیرم: پیشنهاد در کوتاه‌مدت پرهزینه‌ست، حتی اگر استدلال بلندمدتش همچنان خیلی قانع‌کننده باشه."
          }
        ],
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c1_persuasion_concession_scene_2",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-persuasion-concession-02",
        "title": "Persuasion & Concession: part 2",
        "setting": "professional workshop",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "requests",
        "characters": [
          "Elena",
          "Marcus"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Elena",
            "text": "How would you respond without making the disagreement personal?",
            "translation_fa": "چطور جواب می‌دادی بدون اینکه مخالفت شخصی بشه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Marcus",
            "text": "The strongest counterargument is not that the goal is wrong, but that the proposed mechanism may create a new problem.",
            "translation_fa": "قوی‌ترین استدلال مخالف این نیست که هدف غلطه، بلکه اینه که سازوکار پیشنهادی ممکنه مشکل جدیدی ایجاد کنه."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Elena",
            "text": "What could you concede while still holding your position?",
            "translation_fa": "چی رو می‌تونی بپذیری و در عین حال موضعت رو حفظ کنی؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 4,
            "speaker": "Marcus",
            "text": "Our credibility depends on distinguishing what we know from what we merely hope will happen.",
            "translation_fa": "اعتبار ما به این بستگی داره که چیزی رو که می‌دونیم از چیزی که فقط امیدواریم اتفاق بیفته جدا کنیم."
          }
        ],
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c1_persuasion_concession_scene_3",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-persuasion-concession-03",
        "title": "Persuasion & Concession: part 3",
        "setting": "strategy meeting",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "requests",
        "characters": [
          "Hana",
          "Luis"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Hana",
            "text": "What do you make of the way this is being framed?",
            "translation_fa": "از نحوه مطرح شدن این موضوع چه برداشتی داری؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Luis",
            "text": "An emotional appeal may attract attention, but it should not replace evidence where the decision has serious consequences.",
            "translation_fa": "استدلال احساسی ممکنه توجه جلب کنه، ولی جایی که تصمیم پیامد جدی داره نباید جای شواهد رو بگیره."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Hana",
            "text": "Is there another interpretation we should keep in view?",
            "translation_fa": "تفسیر دیگه‌ای هست که باید در نظر داشته باشیم؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 4,
            "speaker": "Luis",
            "text": "I would frame the recommendation around the shared objective, then explain why this option handles the trade-offs better.",
            "translation_fa": "توصیه رو حول هدف مشترک قاب‌بندی می‌کنم و بعد توضیح می‌دم چرا این گزینه تعارض‌ها رو بهتر مدیریت می‌کنه."
          }
        ],
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
